SUMMARY:14th Annual Montclair Bikery Turkey Ride
DESCRIPTION:Following its huge success over the last 13 years\, the Montclair Bikery presents the 14th Annual Turkey Ride benefitting the Human Needs Food Pantry\, taking place on Sunday\, Nov. 22\, 2026. Cyclists will meet at the Montclair Bikery at 148 Valley Road to ride through a lat\, 15-mile circuitous route to the Kings supermarket in Montclair\, where they will buy frozen turkeys and deliver them by bike and by courtesy van to the Human Needs Food Pantry\, also located in Montclair. \nThe donations help the Human Needs Food Pantry distribute over 1\,800 turkeys annually along with all the fixings for a complete Thanksgiving feast to their clients during the week of the holiday. Those who choose not to to ride\, but wish to support the event can donate online at www.humanneedsfoodpantry.org or via the Just Giving link at h ps://www.justgiving.com/campaign/turkeyride2026 . Bulk turkey orders are also available by contacting The Pantry in advance. \nInterested participants are requested to pre-register at www.bikereg.com/Montclair-Bikery-Turkey-Ride or in person at Montclair Bikery starting at 9am. All riders must be 18 years or older\, or 13+with a parent\, and are asked to pay $22 per turkey purchase. The ride begins promptly at 10am. \n“It’s always inspiring to me to see so many people who are willing to give of themselves and share in such a fun event. That helps motivate us to give back to this great community\,” says Dave Adornato\, owner of the Montclair Bikery. \nLast year\, over 350 cyclists enjoyed a beautiful\, cold fall day and donated 1\,400 turkeys to the Human Needs Food Pantry. This year\, the Montclair Bikery is hoping to have 400 cyclists match that figure. Over the last 13 years\, the Turkey Ride has collected over 7\,500 turkeys and raised over $340\,000 for The Pantry. \n“The annual Turkey Ride has become a mainstay for the Thanksgiving holiday here at The Pantry\, helping ensure that we have enough turkeys for all of the people we serve. We are grateful to everyone who organizes the event\, all the generous donors and special thanks to all the riders who brave the elements and deliver the turkeys\,” says Mike Bruno\, Executive Director of the Human Needs Food Pantry. \n“Thanksgiving is one of the few holidays that focuses specifically on giving thanks for all we have and we are thankful for all the caring\, generous people who make this wonderful event happen every year! We are serving more people than ever before in our history and are only able to keep up with the holiday needs because of this event.” \nSNAP benefits continue to be scaled back despite minimal increases\, food prices are still rising and reaching record highs in critical categories and The Pantry is serving nearly 4\,000 clients a month. Food costs are up 33% vs. 2020 which makes life more dif icult for The Pantry’s clients. Already in 2026\, The Pantry has distributed over 800\,000 pounds of food\, costing over $600\,000. \nShare this:\n				Share on Facebook (Opens in new window)\n				Facebook\n			\n				Share on Bluesky (Opens in new window)\n				Bluesky\n			\n				Share on LinkedIn (Opens in new window)\n				LinkedIn\n			\n				Share on Threads (Opens in new window)\n				Threads\n			\n				Share on Nextdoor (Opens in new window)\n				Nextdoor\n			\n				Share on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\n				WhatsApp\n			\n				Email a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\n				Email
URL:https://montclairlocal.news/event/14th-annual-montclair-bikery-turkey-ride/
